Reef backport (docker/patch/sglang_qwen3_5_mrope_rope.patch), applied by
docker/Dockerfile.reef to the SGLang pin f7ea06e1 in /opt/sglang.

The fused Qwen3.5 Q/K norm + RoPE + gate kernel reads only row 0 of the [3, T]
M-RoPE positions. Row 0 is the temporal position. So the kernel rotates image
tokens with the wrong height and width positions.

The first three files carry upstream sgl-project/sglang#34446 (commit
e635577431): the kernel, the axis map in mrope.py and the call in qwen3_5.py.
They use the pin's file paths. The pin's kernel file is the same blob as the
upstream base (56d4420). In mrope.py, the pin keeps its
is_true_on_policy_enabled() check where upstream has _force_native.

The weight_checker.py change is not in upstream. The axis map is now a buffer.
The weight checker's reset_tensors fills every buffer that is not in its skip
list with random values, and a weight update does not restore buffers. The
config sets the axis map, as it sets cos_sin_cache, so the change adds it to
the skip list. Upstream main has the same skip list without axis_map.

Remove this patch, its Dockerfile step and
tests/inference/test_sglang_qwen3_5_mrope.py when the pin contains
e635577431. Check the weight checker skip list of the new pin.

